#pragma once
namespace insim {
inline const char* changelogText() {
    return "What's new in 0.7.10\n\nSmoother scene processing: skip image copies the final scene does not need. This reduces repeated graphics-memory setup. Performance gains vary by scene and computer.\n\nStatus files and live control checks run in the background so slow storage does not hold up rendering. Your saved choices and current FSR, NR and frame-generation options are kept.\n\nThis is a Windows rendering correction. Linux keeps its separate FSR 3.1 preview. Mac rendering is still unavailable.\n\nRetained from 0.7.9:\n\nOptional Discord reports: open Diagnostics, then Preview / send a Discord report. Read the filtered preview, choose a channel and agree before sending. Send now, or once after this session. Cancel before exit to turn the queue Off.\n\nInclude matching X-Plane Log.txt, setup errors, saved image settings and small crash text when available. Original files stay unchanged. Models, DLLs and memory dumps are excluded. Filtering cannot find every private detail, so check the preview.\n\nA Sent status includes a Discord receipt. Uncertain uploads are not repeated automatically. Browser uploads also support Native AA logs. Automatic in-sim submission is Windows-only.\n\nClearer setup and hardware guides, plus a corrected conflict check for empty or disabled known-plugin leftovers. A clean-install warning still needs a fresh log. No new rendering algorithm is added.\n\nRetained from 0.7.8:\n\nRelease includes all current FSR, neural rendering, frame generation and compatibility options. Choose Beta to try upcoming changes. These are the only two update channels. Previous Normal and Experimental selections carry over as Release and Beta.\n\nDownloads now have one clearly named setup executable. Your saved image settings and local models stay in place when updating the same app folder.\n\nRetained from 0.7.7:\n\nSetup now recognizes a verified previous installation of this mod for the same simulator. Updates start with the existing app folder when available. Unknown or edited plugins are still protected.\n\nIf setup fails, it shows the real reason and log location. X-Plane does not have to be running for an ownership error to happen.\n\nRetained from 0.7.6:\n\nLess repeated setup work: the renderer reuses finished image buffers to reduce CPU spikes. This also works when frame generation was enabled at startup and then switched Off.\n\nMore reliable startup: a verified setup link helps the panel find your installation. If needed, Repair startup link fixes the connection. Close and reopen X-Plane after repair.\n\nEasier logs: open Diagnostics > Open log folder. A fresh copy is saved to X-Plane / Output / FSR-Logs after each session.\n\nFirst setup no longer shows a developer's simulator path. Choose your own X-Plane folder. Existing choices are kept.\n\nChoose FSR, independent Native AA or Original simulator as the image processor. Only one mod processes the scene. Restart after switching.\n\nKeep the grouped controls, transitions and help from 0.7.5. The desktop app only updates plugins.\n\nFrame generation pauses while this panel is open. NR and frame generation still cost processing time; this update does not remove every source of stutter.";
}
}
